/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::AnimatedAttributesBase()
\brief Create independently animated drawing attributes.

The default constructor starts with default Attributes and a logical size of 1 by 1. The Attributes overload seeds an immediate sample; no animation tracks are copied.

\see animate(), changeFillColor()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::AnimatedAttributesBase(const Attributes & attributes)
\brief Create independently animated drawing attributes.

The default constructor starts with default Attributes and a logical size of 1 by 1. The Attributes overload seeds an immediate sample; no animation tracks are copied.

\param attributes Attributes value to copy, including its affine transform.

\see animate(), changeFillColor()
*/





/**
\fn bool pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::animate(double seconds)
\brief Advance appearance and transform animation.

Advances programmed movement, scheduled transitions, frame sequences, and animation helpers. Tween pause affects transitions and delays; constant rates still run.

\param seconds Finite nonnegative elapsed time in seconds.

\return True if the update changed animation values; false otherwise.

\note Advance a standalone object with animate(seconds). Drawing and ElementRef copy a sample of Attributes; apply later samples with ElementRef::setAttributes(). MVC controllers advance their Views automatically.

\see AnimatedBase::pauseSchedule(), changeFillColor()
*/



/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeLineColor(const Color & target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
\brief Animate stroke color.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineColor() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Target Color, interpolated component by component.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing EasingFunc callback, such as linearTween or easeInOutQuad. Its elapsed time and duration arguments are seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\note Advance a standalone object with animate(seconds). Drawing and ElementRef copy a sample of Attributes; apply later samples with ElementRef::setAttributes(). MVC controllers advance their Views automatically.

\see lineColor(), AnimatedBase::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeLineThickness(float target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
\brief Animate stroke thickness.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineThickness() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Finite target stroke width in drawing/Port units.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing EasingFunc callback, such as linearTween or easeInOutQuad. Its elapsed time and duration arguments are seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see lineThickness(), AnimatedBase::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeLineOpacity(float target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
\brief Animate stroke opacity.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineOpacity() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Finite target opacity, normally from 0 to 1.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing EasingFunc callback, such as linearTween or easeInOutQuad. Its elapsed time and duration arguments are seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see lineOpacity(), AnimatedBase::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeFillColor(const Color & target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
\brief Animate solid fill color.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate fillColor() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Selects a solid fill and replaces previous solid/gradient fill-color tracks. Fill opacity remains independent.

\param target Target Color, interpolated component by component.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing EasingFunc callback, such as linearTween or easeInOutQuad. Its elapsed time and duration arguments are seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\note Advance a standalone object with animate(seconds). Drawing and ElementRef copy a sample of Attributes; apply later samples with ElementRef::setAttributes(). MVC controllers advance their Views automatically.

\par Example
\code{.cpp}
pdg::AnimatedAttributes<> style;
style.fillColor(pdg::Color(1, 0, 0));
style.changeFillColor(pdg::Color(0, 0, 1), 0.5);
style.animate(0.25);
// Passing style to a Drawing captures this sample, not its animation tracks.
\endcode

\see fillColor(), AnimatedBase::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeFillOpacity(float target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
\brief Animate fill opacity.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate fillOpacity() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue.

\param target Finite target opacity, normally from 0 to 1.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing EasingFunc callback, such as linearTween or easeInOutQuad. Its elapsed time and duration arguments are seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see fillOpacity(), AnimatedBase::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn AnimatedAttributesBase & pdg::AnimatedAttributesBase::changeRoundedCorners(float target, double seconds, EasingFunc easing)
